LICENSE DECISION POINT (M22-M1) — READ BEFORE MERGING AS FINAL.

MIT was chosen as the DEFAULT license because the commander's intent for
Mission 22 is "unblock lawful commercial use" with minimum friction, and MIT
is maximally permissive for a self-hosted product whose differentiation is
operational (governance, audit, sandboxing), not secrecy. THIS IS A
REVERSIBLE DEFAULT, NOT A SETTLED LEGAL POSITION:

  * If dual-licensing / open-core (e.g. Apache-2.0 core + commercial license
    for enterprise features) is preferred, replace this file BEFORE any
    external distribution or paid engagement — license terms apply from first
    distribution, not from first sale.
  * If a copyleft option (AGPL-3.0) is preferred to protect the hosted-service
    surface, swap it here AND re-check every vendored dependency's
    compatibility before shipping.
  * Either way: have counsel confirm the final choice. See also
    [PLACEHOLDER: counsel review] markers in TERMS.md and PRIVACY.md.

Until replaced, the text below is the operative license.
